{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on the least probable outcomes of each lottery, defined as the most favorable outcome with the lowest probability. For Lottery A, the least probable outcome is 3000 Euros with a 25% probability. For Lottery B, it is 4000 Euros with a 20% probability. The reason compares these least probable but most favorable outcomes and prefers the lottery with the more favorable (i.e., higher monetary value) of these outcomes. Since 4000 Euros > 3000 Euros, the decision reason would prefer Lottery B. Thus, the reason can be applied to the decision problem, and the relevant information (the value and probability of the least probable favorable outcome in each lottery) is available.",
