  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on comparing the most favorable outcome with the lowest probability across lotteries. In this case, only Lottery B has such an outcome: 0 Euros with 20%. Lottery A has no variation, so it lacks a least probable outcome. The reason would prefer B due to the presence of a favorable rare outcome. The individual explicitly notes the small chance of avoiding a loss (i.e., getting 0 Euros), which is exactly this favorable rare outcome. Their justification centers on this possibility as a reason to consider B favorably, which aligns with the core logic of the decision reason. While they also mention the downside, their focus on the rare positive outcome as a motivating factor matches the informational focus and evaluative rule of the reason. Therefore, the individual's deliberation reflects the use of the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 95
